<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikandar Begum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a>–<a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikandar-lodi">Sikandar</a> Begum was the ruler of Bhopal State, first as regent and from 1860 as begum in her own right, the second of the four women who governed Bhopal between 1819 and 1926. She reformed its revenue and administration, stayed loyal to the British during the rising of 1857 and in 1863 became the first Indian ruler to perform the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajj">hajj</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikandar-begum.jpg" alt="Sikandar Begum" width="264" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown; subject died 1868. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sikandar_Begum_Bhopal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
